## the brief's own ready command clears the draft, and its readback prints draft: no
$ (cd $LAB/wt && glab-axi mr update 3 --ready)
updated:
  iid: 3
  title: "fixture: GitLab port gate re-validation (throwaway)"
  state: opened
  draft: no
help[1]:
  Run `glab-axi mr view 3 --full` to see updated state
[exit 0]
$ (cd $LAB/wt && glab-axi mr view 3 --full | grep -E '^ *(state|draft|head_sha):')
  state: opened
  draft: no
  head_sha: 7d1d801262fc56fefa967d1ce931cf30a9f6904b
[exit 0]
## S3: with jq, arming the ready merge request records pr= and the forge head as pr_head=
$ fm-pr-check.sh nm-7226-live https://gitlab.com/gh0stwin/firstmate-gitlab-port-fixture/-/merge_requests/3
armed: state/nm-7226-live.check.sh
[exit 0]
$ grep -E '^(pr|pr_head)=' $LAB/state/nm-7226-live.meta
pr=https://gitlab.com/gh0stwin/firstmate-gitlab-port-fixture/-/merge_requests/3
pr_head=7d1d801262fc56fefa967d1ce931cf30a9f6904b
[exit 0]
$ glab mr view 3 -R gh0stwin/firstmate-gitlab-port-fixture -F json | jq -r .sha   # the forge's own head
7d1d801262fc56fefa967d1ce931cf30a9f6904b
[exit 0]
$ git -C $LAB/wt rev-parse HEAD
7d1d801262fc56fefa967d1ce931cf30a9f6904b
[exit 0]
